F_X(x) =
\begin{cases}
    0, & \text{if $x &lt; 0$,} \\
    0.25, & \text{if } 0 \leq x &lt; 1, \\
    0.75, & \text{if } 1 \leq x &lt; 2, \\
    1,   & \text{if } x \geq 2. \\
\end{cases}
}
\]

If \(X\) only takes integer values, its PMF can be obtained from CDF by differencing.
\[
\small{
p_X(k)=\text{P}(X \leq k) - \text{P}(X \leq k-1) = F_X(k) - F_X(k-1)\\
}
\]








\[
\small{
\begin{aligned}
p_X(0)&=F_X(0)-F_X(-1)=0.25-0=0.25 \\
p_X(1)&=F_X(1)-F_X(0)=0.75-0.25=0.5 \\
p_X(2)&=F_X(2)-F_X(1)=1-0.75=0.25 \\
\end{aligned}
}
\]

